  "records": {
    "description": "A collection of three multipliers for multiplying 8/16/32-bit numbers. It uses a looping Carry Save Adder (CSA) design shown in Bennyscubes video. The Carry Save Adders have CCAs attached to them, with the CCA design by Amino. The device runs on a 3rt clock cycle. It also functions on Bedrock by turning the glass blocks (of the CCAs) into upper half slabs.",
    "input": "Two 8 / 16 / 32 bit numbers",
    "output": "16 / 32 / 64 bit Multiplication result",
    "speed": "Runs on a 3rt clock cycle",
    "notes": "On Bedrock, the glass blocks of the CCAs have to be turned into upper half slabs"
  },
